### 1. Register a new user & retrieve JWT
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "settings.test@starkindustries.com",
  "firstName": "Pepper",
  "lastName": "Potts"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("auth_token", response.body.token);
%}

### 2. Save an AI Model Configuration for the user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/models
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "9f4217bf-42dc-44bd-9276-dd1297b54460",
  "name": "gemini-1.5-flash",
  "apiKey": "AIzaSyDummyKeyThatShouldBeSecret123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("modelId", response.body.id);
%}

### 3. Fetch User Settings (Should return 404/Not Found initially)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Accept: application/json


### 4. Set Default Model in User Settings
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/settings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

{
  "defaultModelId": "{{modelId}}"
}


### 5. Fetch User Settings Again (Should return 200 & configured default model)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/users/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Accept: application/json


### 6. Create a Conversation
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat/conversations
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

{
  "title": "Default Model Chat Test"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("conversationId", response.body.id);
%}


### 7. Send message WITHOUT specifying modelId (Resolves default model!)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/chat/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

{
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}",
  "content": "Hello! I am testing default model integration.",
  "senderType": "user"
}
